Careful: recordCompletion returns newlyUnlocked. For daily-3, after three calls: first returns ["first-strokes"], second returns [], third returns ["daily-3"] (since daily-3 rule is events.length>=1 so first-strokes already unlocked). Actually after third call, newly = ["daily-3"]. Let me structure the test to assert final list via getUnlockedAchievements.

Also on-a-roll needs events sorted by ts within 10 min window: `sorted[i].ts - sorted[i-2].ts <= 10*60*1000`. With 3 events at t, t+5min, t+10min → t+10min - t = 10min <= 10min → true.

Negative case: t, t+6min, t+12min → t+12-t=12min > 10min → false; also i=2 checks sorted[2]-sorted[0] only for 3 events. So false. Good.

Note: events array persists across calls via AsyncStorage mock. And same-day dedupe: `dateKey(e.ts) === today` — today from Date.now (clock). Good.

Let me write both tests now.

